# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_resolve_rust_workspace.py" "RUST-WORKSPACE GATE: PASS" "Rust workspace-crate cross-crate import resolution" "Rust workspace-crate import resolution: in a Cargo workspace, a file doing use grep_matcher::Matcher resolves to the workspace member crates/matcher/src/lib.rs instead of staying unresolved (inert). MEASURED on ripgrep: 93 workspace-sibling imports unresolved BEFORE, 5 AFTER (95% recovery, 39 resolved rs-rs edges up to 74). The resolver reads root Cargo.toml for workspace.members (with glob expansion), reads each member Cargo.toml for package.name (plus optional lib.name override), builds a crate-name to src-dir map (hyphens and underscores aliased: grep-matcher and grep_matcher both map to crates/matcher/src), then routes import remainder into the member src directory using the existing suffix-index. PRECISION: crate names not in the workspace map stay unresolved (they are real external deps like std or serde). NEVER-CRASH: missing or malformed Cargo.toml yields empty map, behavior unchanged. Cases proven: basic cross-crate, hyphen-to-underscore normalization, glob member expansion, external crate non-resolve, no-workspace repo inert, intra-crate recall-safe, sub-module cross-crate." "Rust workspace-crate import resolution: 7 cases: basic cross-crate resolve, hyphen-to-underscore name alias, glob expansion of workspace members, external crate stays unresolved (precision), no-workspace repo is inert (never-crash), intra-crate resolve still works (recall-safe), cross-crate with sub-module path" 16
